[141.28, " The harness, fixtures, rules and reference are unchanged. The commands I ran and a summary of the changes are recorded\r\u001b[1B  in \u001b[38;2;87;105;247mNOTES.md\u001b[39m.\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m\u273b\u001b[3GCogitated for 3m 1s \u00b7 done 3:42 PM\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[48;2;240;240;240m\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m\u276f \u001b[38;2;0;0;0mProfile this implementation on the supplied development workloads. Improve performance within the same rules and \u001b[39m     \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;0;0;0mremaining budget. Preserve the interface and correctness requirements. Do not use hidden evaluation inputs, external \u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;0;0;0mimplementations or other ports. Record profiling evidence, changes, tests and remaining limitations in NOTES.md.\u001b[39m      \r\u001b[6C\u001b[2B\u001b[49m\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m\u001b[1m4\r\u001b[2C\u001b[2B\u001b[22m\u001b[39mMatmul\u001b[11Gare\u001b[15G~12.4 ms of the\u001b[31G13.5 ms forward, all running at ~35 GB/s regardless of layout. Let me check\u001b[107Gwhether that's\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bthe \u001b[8Gemory ceiling\u001b[22Gor a BLAS-ke\u001b[35Gnel limit.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B \u001b[3G\u001b[38;2;102;102;102mRan \u001b[1m2\u001b[22m "]
