[624.81, "\u001b[H\r\u001b[41C\u001b[33B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102mthought for 7s)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[40;1H\u001b[38;3H"]
[624.827, "\u001b[H\r\u001b[33B\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m\u2733\u001b[4Gi\u001b[39m\u001b[40;1H\u001b[38;3H"]
[624.843, "\u001b[H\r\u001b[28B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m\u23fa\u001b[39m\u001b[40;1H\u001b[38;3H"]
[624.858, "\u001b]0;\u25d0 Claude Code\u0007"]
[624.898, "\u001b[H\u001b[6G\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;0;0;0m\u23fa\u001b[3G\u001b[39mI\u001b[5Gclaimed in NOTES that no vocab score falls in that merge-floor range; checking:\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102mRan \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shell command \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;0;0;0m\u23fa\u001b[3G\u001b[39mEach token's forward pass is about 20\u201325% faster than the first version: around \u001b[1m11.0 ms instead of 13.6\u201314.9 ms\u001b[115G\u001b[22mon\u001b[118Gthe\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bsupplied prompts. Encoding long prompts is now about 150\u00d7 faster. Both \u001b[38;2;87;105;247mcheck.py\u001b[39m runs still pass, the quick one and\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bthe full one (3 prompts, 64 tokens), with a largest logit error of 2.7e-5 against the 5e-4 limit.\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mWhat the profiling showed\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5GIn the first version, the matrix-vector products took 12.4 ms of the 13.5 ms per token. That's reading the 438\u001b[116GMB\u001b[119Gof\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bweights at about 35 GB/s, so speed is limited by memory reads, not arithmetic.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5GNumPy's \u001b[38;2;87;105;247mnp.vecdot\u001b[39m reads the same weights at 43\u201347 GB/s"]
[624.9, ", versus about 35 GB/s for Accelerate's matrix-vector routine\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B(\u001b[38;2;87;105;247mnp.dot\u001b[39m). It does the same row-by-row float32 dot products with about the same rounding error.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5GThe prompt tokenizer took time proportional to the square of the prompt length: 770 ms for a 1,021-token prompt,\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bwhich costs as much as about 70 forward passes.\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mChanges\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B1.\u001b[6GAll matrix-vector products now use \u001b[38;2;87;105;247mnp.vecdot\u001b[39m, still as separate calls with the same shapes. That part of each\u001b[116Gtoken\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bwent from 12.4 ms to 10.4 ms.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B2.\u001b[6GK and V are written directly into their slot in the cache, and the position rotation (RoPE) is done there as\u001b[115Ga\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bfloat32 complex multiply using the reference formula. I also removed temporary arrays and extra calls. Other\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bper-token work fell from about 1.1 ms to 0.5 ms, and everything stays float32.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B3.\u001b[6GThe tokenizer's merge step now picks merges from a priorit"]
[624.901, "y queue, in exactly the order the reference loop picks\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bthem. It gave identical token ids on 3,009 test inputs. A 1,021-token prompt now encodes in 4.8 ms instead of\u001b[116G770\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bms.\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BOver\u001b[8Gthe\u001b[12Gfull\u001b[17Gcommand\u001b[25Gprotocol\u001b[34G(best\u001b[40Gof\u001b[43G2\u001b[45Gruns),\u001b[52Gthe\u001b[56Gtotal\u001b[62Gwent\u001b[67Gfrom\u001b[72G22.9\u001b[77Gs\u001b[79Gto\u001b[82G18.7\u001b[87Gs.\u001b[90GThe\u001b[94G1,021-token\u001b[106Gprompt\u001b[113Grun\r\u001b[1B \u001b[3Gdropped\u001b[11Gfrom 16.3 s to 13.0\u001b[31Gs.\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mNot done\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mCombining weight matrices:\u001b[32G\u001b[22mmerging\u001b[40GQ/K/V\u001b[46Gand\u001b[50GW1/W3\u001b[56Ginto\u001b[61Gsingle\u001b[68Gcalls\u001b[74Gsaves\u001b[80Gonly\u001b[85Gabout\u001b[91G0.3\u001b[95Gms\u001b[98Gper\u001b[102Gtoken.\u001b[109GIt\u001b[112Gwould\r\u001b[1B \u001b[3G  need about 270 MB of copying at load, which loses on\u001b[58Gshort\u001b[64Gruns.\r\u001b[1B  -\u001b[K\u001b[40;1H\u001b[38;3H"]
[625.042, "\u001b[H\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102mRan \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shell command \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;0;0;0m\u23fa\u001b[3G\u001b[39mEach\u001b[8Gtoken's\u001b[16Gforward\u001b[24Gpass\u001b[29Gis\u001b[32Gabout\u001b[38G20\u201325%\u001b[45Gfaster\u001b[52Gthan\u001b[57Gthe\u001b[61Gfirst\u001b[67Gversion:\u001b[76Garound\u001b[83G\u001b[1m11.0 ms instead of 13.6\u201314.9 ms\u001b[115G\u001b[22mon\u001b[118Gthe\r\u001b[1B \u001b[3Gsupplied prompts. Encoding long prompts is now about 150\u00d7\u001b[62Gaster. Both \u001b[38;2;87;105;247mcheck.py\u001b[83G\u001b[39mruns still pass, the quick one and\u001b[118G\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bthe full\u001b[12Gone (3 prompts, 64 tokens), with a largest logit\u001b[61Gerror of 2.7e-5 against the 5e-4\u001b[94Glimit.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mWhat the profiling showed\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[22m- In the first version, the\u001b[31Gmatrix-vector\u001b[45Gproducts\u001b[54Gtook\u001b[59G12.4\u001b[64Gms\u001b[67Gof\u001b[70Gthe\u001b[74G13.5\u001b[79Gms\u001b[82Gper\u001b[86Gtoken.\u001b[93GThat's\u001b[100Greading\u001b[108Gthe\u001b[112G438\u001b[116GMB\u001b[119Gof\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B \u001b[5Gweig\u001b[10Gts at about 35 GB/s,\u001b[31Gso speed is limited by\u001b[54Gmemory read\u001b[66G, no\u001b[71G arithmetic.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5GNumPy'\u001b[13G\u001b[38;2;87;105;247mnp.vecdot\u001b[39m read"]
[625.044, "s the sam\u001b[37G we\u001b[41Gghts a\u001b[48G 43\u201347 GB/s,\u001b[61Gv\u001b[63Grsus\u001b[68Gabout 35 GB/s for\u001b[86GAccelerate's\u001b[99Gmatrix-vector\u001b[113Groutine\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B \u001b[5G(\u001b[38;2;87;105;247mnp.dot\u001b[39m). It does\u001b[23Gthe \u001b[28Game row-by-row flo\u001b[48G32 dot\u001b[55Gproducts with about the same \u001b[85Gounding error.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5GThe prompt \u001b[17Gokenizer took time prop\u001b[41Grtion\u001b[47Gl to the square of \u001b[68Ge promp\u001b[76G length: 770 ms fo\u001b[95G a 1,021-token\u001b[110Gprompt,\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B \u001b[5Gw\u001b[7Gich cos\u001b[15Gs as much as about 70 f\u001b[39Grward p\u001b[47Gsses.\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mChanges\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[22m1. All matrix-vector\u001b[24Gproducts\u001b[33Gnow\u001b[37Guse\u001b[41G\u001b[38;2;87;105;247mnp.vecdot\u001b[39m,\u001b[52Gstill\u001b[58Gas\u001b[61Gseparate\u001b[70Gcalls\u001b[76Gwith\u001b[81Gthe\u001b[85Gsame\u001b[90Gshapes.\u001b[98GThat\u001b[103Gpart\u001b[108Gof\u001b[111Geach\u001b[116Gtoken\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  \u001b[6Gwent from 12.4 ms\u001b[24Gto 10.4 ms.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B2.\u001b[6GK and V are written directly into\u001b[40Gtheir\u001b[46Gslot\u001b[51Gin\u001b[54Gthe\u001b[58Gcache,\u001b[65Gand\u001b[69Gthe\u001b[73Gposition\u001b[82Grotation\u001b[91G(RoPE)\u001b[98Gis\u001b[101Gdone\u001b[106Gthere\u001b[112Gas\u001b[115Ga\r\u001b[2C\u001b["]
[625.046, "1B  \u001b[6Gfloat32\u001b[14Gcomplex multiply using \u001b[38Ghe r\u001b[43Gference\u001b[51Gformula. I also removed temp\u001b[80Gra\u001b[83Gy \u001b[86Grrays and extra calls. Other\u001b[115G\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bper-\u001b[11Goken work fel\u001b[25G from\u001b[31Gabout\u001b[37G1.1\u001b[41Gms to 0.5\u001b[51Gms, and everything stays float32.\u001b[85G\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B3.\u001b[6GThe \u001b[15Gize\u001b[19G's merge step now\u001b[37Gpicks merges from\u001b[56G priority queue, in\u001b[76Gexac\u001b[81Gly the\u001b[88Gorder\u001b[94Gthe\u001b[98Greference\u001b[108Gloop\u001b[113Gpicks\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  \u001b[6Gt\u001b[9Gm. It gave identical token ids on\u001b[43G3,009 test inputs. A 1,021-toke\u001b[76Gprompt now encodes in\u001b[98G4.8 ms instead\u001b[113Gof 770\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bms.\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BOver\u001b[8Gthe\u001b[12Gfull\u001b[17Gcommand\u001b[25Gprotocol\u001b[34G(best\u001b[40Gof\u001b[43G2\u001b[45Gruns),\u001b[52Gthe\u001b[56Gtotal\u001b[62Gwent\u001b[67Gfrom\u001b[72G22.9\u001b[77Gs\u001b[79Gto\u001b[82G18.7\u001b[87Gs.\u001b[90GThe\u001b[94G1,021-token\u001b[106Gprompt\u001b[113Grun\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bdropped from 16.3 s to 13.0 s.\u001b[34G\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mNot done\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mCombining weight matrices:\u001b[32G\u001b[22mmerging\u001b[40GQ/K/V\u001b[46Gand\u001b[50GW1/W3\u001b[56Ginto\u001b[61Gsing"]
[625.047, "le\u001b[68Gcalls\u001b[74Gsaves\u001b[80Gonly\u001b[85Gabout\u001b[91G0.3\u001b[95Gms\u001b[98Gper\u001b[102Gtoken.\u001b[109GIt\u001b[112Gwould\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B \u001b[5Gneed about 270 MB of copying at load, which loses on short runs.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mTransposed weights:\u001b[22m similar speed, but 5\u20137\u00d7\u001b[49Gm\u001b[51Gr\u001b[53G r\u001b[56Gunding e\u001b[65Gror\u001b[40;1H\u001b[38;3H"]
[625.232, "\u001b[H\r\u001b[4C\u001b[34B\u001b[1mProcessing the whole prompt at once:\u001b[42G\u001b[22mreading\u001b[50Gthe\u001b[54Gweights\u001b[62Gonce\u001b[67Gper\u001b[71Gprompt\u001b[78Ginstead\u001b[86Gof\u001b[89Gonce\u001b[94Gper\u001b[98Gtoken\u001b[104Gwould\u001b[110Gbe\u001b[113Gmuch\u001b[40;1H\u001b[38;3H"]
[625.807, "\u001b[H\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102mRan \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shell command \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;0;0;0m\u23fa\u001b[3G\u001b[39mEach\u001b[8Gtoken's\u001b[16Gforward\u001b[24Gpass\u001b[29Gis\u001b[32Gabout\u001b[38G20\u201325%\u001b[45Gfaster\u001b[52Gthan\u001b[57Gthe\u001b[61Gfirst\u001b[67Gversion:\u001b[76Garound\u001b[83G\u001b[1m11.0 ms instead of 13.6\u201314.9 ms\u001b[115G\u001b[22mon\u001b[118Gthe\r\u001b[1B \u001b[3Gsupplied prompts. Encoding long prompts is now about 150\u00d7\u001b[62Gaster. Both \u001b[38;2;87;105;247mcheck.py\u001b[83G\u001b[39mruns still pass, the quick one and\u001b[118G\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bthe full\u001b[12Gone (3 prompts, 64 tokens), with a largest logit\u001b[61Gerror of 2.7e-5 against the 5e-4\u001b[94Glimit.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mWhat the profiling showed\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[22m- In the first version, the\u001b[31Gmatrix-vector\u001b[45Gproducts\u001b[54Gtook\u001b[59G12.4\u001b[64Gms\u001b[67Gof\u001b[70Gthe\u001b[74G13.5\u001b[79Gms\u001b[82Gper\u001b[86Gtoken.\u001b[93GThat's\u001b[100Greading\u001b[108Gthe\u001b[112G438\u001b[116GMB\u001b[119Gof\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B \u001b[5Gweig\u001b[10Gts at about 35 GB/s,\u001b[31Gso speed is limited by\u001b[54Gmemory read\u001b[66G, no\u001b[71G arithmetic.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5GNumPy'\u001b[13G\u001b[38;2;87;105;247mnp.vecdot\u001b[39m reads the sa"]
[625.808, "m\u001b[37G we\u001b[41Gghts a\u001b[48G 43\u201347 GB/s,\u001b[61Gv\u001b[63Grsus\u001b[68Gabout 35 GB/s for\u001b[86GAccelerate's\u001b[99Gmatrix-vector\u001b[113Groutine\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B \u001b[5G(\u001b[38;2;87;105;247mnp.dot\u001b[39m). It does\u001b[23Gthe \u001b[28Game row-by-row flo\u001b[48G32 dot\u001b[55Gproducts with about the same \u001b[85Gounding error.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5GThe prompt \u001b[17Gokenizer took time prop\u001b[41Grtion\u001b[47Gl to the square of \u001b[68Ge promp\u001b[76G length: 770 ms fo\u001b[95G a 1,021-token\u001b[110Gprompt,\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B \u001b[5Gw\u001b[7Gich cos\u001b[15Gs as much as about 70 f\u001b[39Grward p\u001b[47Gsses.\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mChanges\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[22m1. All matrix-vector\u001b[24Gproducts\u001b[33Gnow\u001b[37Guse\u001b[41G\u001b[38;2;87;105;247mnp.vecdot\u001b[39m,\u001b[52Gstill\u001b[58Gas\u001b[61Gseparate\u001b[70Gcalls\u001b[76Gwith\u001b[81Gthe\u001b[85Gsame\u001b[90Gshapes.\u001b[98GThat\u001b[103Gpart\u001b[108Gof\u001b[111Geach\u001b[116Gtoken\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  \u001b[6Gwent from 12.4 ms\u001b[24Gto 10.4 ms.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B2.\u001b[6GK and V are written directly into\u001b[40Gtheir\u001b[46Gslot\u001b[51Gin\u001b[54Gthe\u001b[58Gcache,\u001b[65Gand\u001b[69Gthe\u001b[73Gposition\u001b[82Grotation\u001b[91G(RoPE)\u001b[98Gis\u001b[101Gdone\u001b[106Gthere\u001b[112Gas\u001b[115Ga\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  \u001b[6G"]
[625.809, "float32\u001b[14Gcomplex multiply using \u001b[38Ghe r\u001b[43Gference\u001b[51Gformula. I also removed temp\u001b[80Gra\u001b[83Gy \u001b[86Grrays and extra calls. Other\u001b[115G\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bper-\u001b[11Goken work fel\u001b[25G from\u001b[31Gabout\u001b[37G1.1\u001b[41Gms to 0.5\u001b[51Gms, and everything stays float32.\u001b[85G\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B3.\u001b[6GThe \u001b[15Gize\u001b[19G's merge step now\u001b[37Gpicks merges from\u001b[56G priority queue, in\u001b[76Gexac\u001b[81Gly the\u001b[88Gorder\u001b[94Gthe\u001b[98Greference\u001b[108Gloop\u001b[113Gpicks\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  \u001b[6Gt\u001b[9Gm. It gave identical token ids on\u001b[43G3,009 test inputs. A 1,021-toke\u001b[76Gprompt now encodes in\u001b[98G4.8 ms instead\u001b[113Gof 770\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bms.\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BOver\u001b[8Gthe\u001b[12Gfull\u001b[17Gcommand\u001b[25Gprotocol\u001b[34G(best\u001b[40Gof\u001b[43G2\u001b[45Gruns),\u001b[52Gthe\u001b[56Gtotal\u001b[62Gwent\u001b[67Gfrom\u001b[72G22.9\u001b[77Gs\u001b[79Gto\u001b[82G18.7\u001b[87Gs.\u001b[90GThe\u001b[94G1,021-token\u001b[106Gprompt\u001b[113Grun\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bdropped from 16.3 s to 13.0 s.\u001b[34G\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mNot done\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mCombining weight matrices:\u001b[32G\u001b[22mmerging\u001b[40GQ/K/V\u001b[46Gand\u001b[50GW1/W3\u001b[56Ginto\u001b[61Gsingle\u001b[68Gc"]
[625.81, "alls\u001b[74Gsaves\u001b[80Gonly\u001b[85Gabout\u001b[91G0.3\u001b[95Gms\u001b[98Gper\u001b[102Gtoken.\u001b[109GIt\u001b[112Gwould\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B \u001b[5Gneed about 270 MB of copying at load, which loses on short runs.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mTransposed weights:\u001b[22m similar speed, but 5\u20137\u00d7\u001b[49Gm\u001b[51Gr\u001b[53G r\u001b[56Gunding e\u001b[65Gror\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mP\u001b[7Gocessing\u001b[16Gthe whole prompt at once:\u001b[22m reading th\u001b[54Gweights once per\u001b[71Gprompt\u001b[78Ginstead\u001b[86Gof\u001b[89Gonce\u001b[94Gper\u001b[98Gtoken\u001b[104Gwould\u001b[110Gbe\u001b[113Gmuch\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B \u001b[5Gfaster. I didn't do it because the rul\u001b[44Gs requir\u001b[54Gbatc\u001b[59G \u001b[61Gize 1\u001b[67Gand\u001b[71Gthe reference's cache-filling order. If you read\u001b[40;1H\u001b[38;3H"]
