[626.61, "\u001b[H\u001b[3G\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mWhat the profiling showed\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5GIn\u001b[8Gthe\u001b[12Gfirst\u001b[18Gversion,\u001b[27Gthe\u001b[31Gmatrix-vector\u001b[45Gproducts\u001b[54Gtook\u001b[59G12.4\u001b[64Gms\u001b[67Gof\u001b[70Gthe\u001b[74G13.5\u001b[79Gms\u001b[82Gper\u001b[86Gtoken.\u001b[93GThat's\u001b[100Greading\u001b[108Gthe\u001b[112G438\u001b[116GMB\u001b[119Gof\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  weights at about 35 GB/s,\u001b[31Gso\u001b[34Gspeed\u001b[40Gis\u001b[43Glimited\u001b[51Gby\u001b[54Gmemory\u001b[61Greads,\u001b[68Gnot\u001b[72Garithmetic.\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1BNumPy's \u001b[38;2;87;105;247mnp.vecdot\u001b[39m reads the same w\u001b[40Gights at 43\u201347 GB/s, versus about\u001b[74G35 GB/\u001b[82Gfo\u001b[86GAcc\u001b[90Glerate's matrix-vector routine\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B(\u001b[38;2;87;105;247mnp.dot\u001b[39m). It does the same row-by-row\u001b[43Gfloa\u001b[48G32\u001b[51Gdot pr\u001b[58Gducts with about \u001b[77Ge same\u001b[84Grounding\u001b[93Gerror.\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1BThe prompt tokenizer took time proportion\u001b[47Gl\u001b[49Gto the square of the prompt\u001b[77Glength: 770 ms for a 1,021-tok\u001b[108Gn p\u001b[112Gompt,\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bwhich costs as much as \u001b[29Gbout 70 fo\u001b[40Gward p\u001b[47Gsses.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mChanges\u001b[11G\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B1.\u001b[6GAll\u001b[10Gmatrix-vector\u001b[24"]
